  "id": "Compound::DB00328 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Indomethacin and Slc22a6, primarily through the involvement of Slc22a7 in transport processes. Indomethacin binds to Slc22a7, which is involved in organic anion transport, and this transport process is also associated with Slc22a6. Additionally, Indomethacin is included in the class of nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory compounds, which includes Sulindac, a compound that binds to Slc22a6. This indicates that Indomethacin may influence Slc22a6 through a shared pathway involving transport mechanisms. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, with varying degrees of support from different pathways. The evidence highlights the role of Slc22a7 as a mediator in the transport of anions and zwitterions, which could be relevant to the transport of Indomethacin and other compounds. The integration of these pathways suggests that Indomethacin may interact with Slc22a6 via a transport mechanism, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm this hypothesis.",
